<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One printed page, a single column of italic verse in seven stanzas of four lines, indented in turn. Running head at top right, page number at top left, catchword at lower right. Faint show-through from the other side on the right.</layout>
  <page_number>246</page_number>
  <running_head>CANTICA SACRA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Per</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Quæ grata sedes, quæ tua ciuitas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Dilecta quondam, nunc lapidum iacet</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Turpes acerui, nunc sepulta</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>est Ipsa suis Solymæ ruinis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">
      <i>Passim piorum strata cadauera</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Sunt esca cælifassa[?] volucribus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Carnesque sanctorum tuorum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Præda feris, canibusque terræ,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Fluxere rivi sanguinis undique,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Ut vilis undæ flumina per vias</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Proiecta, nec vili repertus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Corpora qui tegeret sepulcro.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" para="true">
      <i>Turpis propinquis fabula gentibus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Turpis per vrbes finitimas locus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Facti fumus, quis finis irae?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Quo tuus usque vorax ut ignis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Ardebit, ô Rex, horribilis furor?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Exerce in illum sœuitiam tui</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Cœtum flagelli, rite qui te</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Nosse negat, negat invocare.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Nam deuorarunt fauctibus impijs</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Carnes Iacobi. Cinibus oppida</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Agri colonis, templa vasis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Quæque suis spoliata lugent.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25" para="true">
      <i>Ne pristinarum, ne memor amplius</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Sis noxiarum, quas tibi fecimus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Extrema sed passis malorum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Ferre pius propera lenamen[?].</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Stanza breaks follow the four-line pattern of the printed verse. Line 6, "cælifassa[?]", is doubtful: the word is set in a long-s ligature and I could not read it with certainty. Line 28, "lenamen[?]", appears to read so in print; it may be a printing error for "levamen", left as printed. Line 3 "acerui" and line 23 "vasis" are read from the long-s forms and are otherwise clear. The faint text on the right is show-through from the reverse and is omitted.</notes>
</page>
